            <td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:28px 32px;
                       font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#212121;">

              <p>Hello fox hunters,</p>

              <p>
                Our fox hunt planning, event documentation, and equipment
                build resources are now available on GitHub for anyone
                to view and contribute to.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                What's in the Repository?
              </h3>

              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Event planning documents</strong> &mdash;
                  location scouting reports, hunt area boundaries,
                  park rules, and event logistics
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Build instructions</strong> &mdash;
                  step-by-step guides for tape-measure Yagi antennas,
                  attenuators, and other fox hunting equipment
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Email announcement templates</strong> &mdash;
                  draft emails for upcoming events (like the ones
                  sent to this list)
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Presentation materials</strong> &mdash;
                  club meeting presentations and speaker notes
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Post-hunt reports</strong> &mdash;
                  results, photos, and lessons learned from past events
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                How to Access
              </h3>

              <p style="text-align:center;margin:20px 0;">
                <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/ham-fox-hunting"
                   style="display:inline-block;background-color:#1a3a5c;
                          color:#ffffff;padding:12px 24px;
                          text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;
                          font-weight:bold;font-size:16px;">
                  Visit the GitHub Repository
                </a>
              </p>

              <p style="font-size:13px;color:#555555;text-align:center;">
                <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/ham-fox-hunting"
                   style="color:#1a3a5c;">
                  github.com/tsayles/ham-fox-hunting
                </a>
              </p>

              <p>
                The repository is public &mdash; no GitHub account
                required to browse. All documentation is written in
                plain text Markdown, making it easy to read directly
                on GitHub or download for offline reference.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                How to Contribute
              </h3>

              <p>
                Have ideas for improving hunt locations? Better build
                instructions? Photos from a past hunt? Suggestions for
                new equipment? <strong>We welcome contributions!</strong>
              </p>

              <p>
                Here's how to participate:
              </p>

              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Submit a Pull Request</strong> &mdash;
                  if you're familiar with Git/GitHub, fork the repo,
                  make your changes, and submit a PR. We'll review
                  and merge useful contributions.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Open an Issue</strong> &mdash;
                  report problems, suggest improvements, or ask
                  questions using GitHub Issues (no coding required).
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Email suggestions</strong> &mdash;
                  not comfortable with GitHub? Send ideas, corrections,
                  or files directly to
                  <a href="mailto:TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com">TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com</a>
                  and I'll incorporate them.
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Why Open Source?
              </h3>

              <p>
                Open documentation means:
              </p>

              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Transparency</strong> &mdash; everyone can
                  see hunt planning decisions and safety considerations
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Collaboration</strong> &mdash; leverage the
                  collective knowledge of our community
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Reusability</strong> &mdash; other clubs can
                  adapt our materials for their own fox hunt programs
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Version control</strong> &mdash; track changes
                  over time and never lose historical documentation
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Permanence</strong> &mdash; the repository
                  remains accessible even if individual organizers change
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Getting Started with GitHub
              </h3>

              <p>
                New to GitHub? Here are some resources:
              </p>

              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  GitHub's <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/get-started"
                     style="color:#1a3a5c;">Getting Started Guide</a>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests"
                     style="color:#1a3a5c;">How to Submit a Pull Request</a>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <a href="https://www.markdownguide.org/basic-syntax/"
                     style="color:#1a3a5c;">Markdown Syntax Guide</a>
                </li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                Or reach out &mdash; I'm happy to help anyone get started
                with contributing, whether you're a Git expert or have
                never used version control before.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                What's Next?
              </h3>

              <p>
                As we prepare for the August and September hunts, all
                planning documents and event materials will be kept
                up-to-date in the repository. Watch the repo (click
                "Watch" on GitHub) to get notifications when new
                content is added.
              </p>

              <p>
                Questions about the repository or how to contribute?
                Contact <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                <a href="mailto:TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com">TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com</a>
                or reply to this message.
              </p>

              <p>73,<br>Tom Sayles, KE4HET<br>Fox Hunt Program Coordinator</p>

